{% doc %}
  @prompt
    Create a brand-new responsive Shopify section from scratch called “What You Can Expect.”
    
    Do not edit, reuse, or reference the previous section. Build a completely new section.
    
    Use the uploaded reference image as the exact visual guide. Match its mobile layout, proportions, spacing, rounded corners, image placement, phase labels, text-panel sizing, and overall visual hierarchy as closely as possible.
    
    Section heading
    
    Display the heading on one centered line:
    
    WHAT YOU CAN EXPECT
    
    Style it exactly like the reference:
    
    “WHAT YOU CAN” should be dark black or very dark purple.
    “EXPECT” should be Ariya purple #7D45C6.
    Use bold, uppercase, clean sans-serif lettering.
    Make the colored word part of the same heading, not a separate line.
    Keep the heading strong and visually noticeable without taking up excessive vertical space.
    
    Recommended mobile size: approximately 30–34px.
    
    Supporting sentence
    
    Place this centered directly below the heading:
    
    One complete formula to help get your nights—and mornings—back on track.
    
    Keep it:
    
    smaller than the heading
    dark purple or black
    centered
    approximately two lines on mobile
    easy to read
    compact, with no excessive spacing
    
    Recommended mobile size: approximately 17–19px.
    
    Mobile layout
    
    Re-create the three stacked phase rows exactly like the reference image.
    
    Each phase must be one horizontal rounded row containing:
    
    an image area on the left
    a description panel on the right
    a purple phase label attached directly underneath the image
    
    Do not stack the image above the description.
    
    Row proportions
    Left image-and-label column: approximately 31–33% of the row width.
    Right description panel: approximately 67–69% of the row width.
    The image, label, and description panel must touch with no gaps between them.
    The full row should have rounded outer corners.
    Keep each row compact, approximately 185–210px tall on mobile.
    No row should become an oversized vertical block.
    Left image area
    Display the uploaded image at the top of the left column.
    Use object-fit: cover.
    Crop the image cleanly so it fills the available area.
    Keep the image attached directly to the purple phase label.
    Round only the appropriate outer top corners.
    Do not place text, discount circles, promotional badges, or other overlays on the image.
    Attached phase label
    
    Attach a purple label directly underneath each image.
    
    Requirements:
    
    Background color: Ariya purple #7D45C6.
    Text color: white.
    Label width must exactly match the image width.
    There must be no gap between the image and label.
    The label should look built into the image column.
    Center-align all label text.
    Round the bottom-left outer corner.
    
    Inside each label, use two lines:
    
    Phase name on the first line, larger and bold.
    Time period on the second line, smaller but still clearly readable.
    Phase content
    Phase 1
    
    Purple label:
    
    Phase 1
    First Few Nights
    
    Description:
    
    The calming botanicals begin supporting a quieter mind, helping your body ease into bedtime.
    
    Phase 2
    
    Purple label:
    
    Phase 2
    Weeks 1–2
    
    Description:
    
    As it becomes part of your routine, sleep may feel deeper and nighttime wake-ups less frequent.
    
    Phase 3
    
    Purple label:
    
    Phase 3
    Around 30 Days
    
    Description:
    
    With consistent use, better nights can support clearer, refreshed mornings—without melatonin or next-day grogginess.
    
    Right description panel
    
    Match the reference image closely:
    
    Use a very light lavender background, approximately #F4EEFA.
    Use dark black or deep purple text.
    Vertically center the description inside the panel.
    Left-align the description.
    Use comfortable but compact internal padding.
    Recommended mobile padding: 18–22px.
    Recommended mobile font size: 16–18px.
    Use a line height of approximately 1.35–1.45.
    Round the top-right and bottom-right outer corners.
    Do not use a border.
    Do not use a heavy shadow.
    Do not place titles above the description inside this panel.
    Row spacing
    Keep approximately 14–18px between each phase row.
    Keep all three rows the same width.
    Keep the image columns the same width.
    Keep the purple labels the same height.
    Keep the rows visually aligned and consistent.
    Do not add excessive white space above, below, or between the rows.
    Overall section styling
    Use a white background.
    Keep the content centered.
    Use approximately 20–24px of side padding on mobile.
    Use approximately 32–40px of top padding.
    Use approximately 30–36px of bottom padding.
    Do not use timeline dots.
    Do not use connecting lines.
    Do not use separate bordered cards.
    Do not add floating icons.
    Do not add decorative stars, moons, or animations.
    Do not add a large box around the entire section.
    The visual life should come from the images, colored heading word, purple phase labels, and lavender description panels.
    Desktop layout
    
    Keep the same content and styling, but display the three phases in three equal-width columns on desktop.
    
    For desktop:
    
    Place the image at the top of each column.
    Attach the purple phase label directly underneath the image.
    Place the description underneath.
    Keep all three c, make the headline one single line, make the headline one single line by making it smaller, make the headline one single line by making it smaller on mobile version only, on the mobile version only put the headline, what you can expect in one single line, the time periods make sure they are all on one line
{% enddoc %}
{% assign ai_gen_id = block.id | replace: '_', '' | downcase %}

{% style %}
  .ai-expect-section-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    display: block;
    background-color: {{ block.settings.background_color }};
    padding: {{ block.settings.padding_top_mobile }}px {{ block.settings.padding_horizontal_mobile }}px {{ block.settings.padding_bottom_mobile }}px;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .ai-expect-section-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      padding: {{ block.settings.padding_top_desktop }}px {{ block.settings.padding_horizontal_desktop }}px {{ block.settings.padding_bottom_desktop }}px;
    }
  }

  .ai-expect-container-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .ai-expect-header-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: {{ block.settings.header_spacing_mobile }}px;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .ai-expect-header-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      margin-bottom: {{ block.settings.header_spacing_desktop }}px;
    }
  }

  .ai-expect-heading-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    font-size: {{ block.settings.heading_size_mobile }}px;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin: 0 0 {{ block.settings.subtext_spacing }}px;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .ai-expect-heading-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      font-size: {{ block.settings.heading_size_desktop }}px;
      white-space: normal;
    }
  }

  .ai-expect-heading-{{ ai_gen_id }} .ai-expect-heading-normal-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    color: {{ block.settings.heading_color }};
  }

  .ai-expect-heading-{{ ai_gen_id }} .ai-expect-heading-accent-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    color: {{ block.settings.heading_accent_color }};
  }

  .ai-expect-subtext-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    font-size: {{ block.settings.subtext_size_mobile }}px;
    color: {{ block.settings.subtext_color }};
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.4;
    max-width: 600px;
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .ai-expect-subtext-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      font-size: {{ block.settings.subtext_size_desktop }}px;
    }
  }

  .ai-expect-phases-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: {{ block.settings.row_spacing }}px;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .ai-expect-phases-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      flex-direction: row;
      gap: {{ block.settings.column_spacing }}px;
    }
  }

  .ai-expect-phase-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    border-radius: {{ block.settings.row_border_radius }}px;
    overflow: hidden;
    height: {{ block.settings.row_height_mobile }}px;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .ai-expect-phase-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      flex-direction: column;
      flex: 1;
      height: auto;
    }
  }

  .ai-expect-image-column-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    width: {{ block.settings.image_width_percent }}%;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .ai-expect-image-column-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      width: 100%;
    }
  }

  .ai-expect-image-wrapper-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    position: relative;
    flex-grow: 1;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-top-left-radius: {{ block.settings.row_border_radius }}px;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .ai-expect-image-wrapper-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      border-top-left-radius: {{ block.settings.row_border_radius }}px;
      border-top-right-radius: {{ block.settings.row_border_radius }}px;
      border-bottom-left-radius: 0;
    }
  }

  .ai-expect-image-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
  }

  .ai-expect-image-placeholder-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    background-color: #f4f4f4;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .ai-expect-image-placeholder-{{ ai_gen_id }} svg {
    width: 60%;
    height: 60%;
    opacity: 0.3;
  }

  .ai-expect-label-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    background-color: {{ block.settings.label_background_color }};
    color: {{ block.settings.label_text_color }};
    text-align: center;
    padding: {{ block.settings.label_padding_vertical }}px {{ block.settings.label_padding_horizontal }}px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: {{ block.settings.row_border_radius }}px;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .ai-expect-label-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      border-bottom-left-radius: 0;
    }
  }

  .ai-expect-label-name-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    font-size: {{ block.settings.label_name_size }}px;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .ai-expect-label-time-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    font-size: {{ block.settings.label_time_size }}px;
    margin: 2px 0 0;
    line-height: 1.2;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .ai-expect-description-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    background-color: {{ block.settings.description_background_color }};
    color: {{ block.settings.description_text_color }};
    padding: {{ block.settings.description_padding_mobile }}px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    flex-grow: 1;
    border-top-right-radius: {{ block.settings.row_border_radius }}px;
    border-bottom-right-radius: {{ block.settings.row_border_radius }}px;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .ai-expect-description-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      padding: {{ block.settings.description_padding_desktop }}px;
      border-top-right-radius: 0;
      border-bottom-left-radius: {{ block.settings.row_border_radius }}px;
    }
  }

  .ai-expect-description-text-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    font-size: {{ block.settings.description_size_mobile }}px;
    line-height: {{ block.settings.description_line_height }};
    margin: 0;
    text-align: left;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .ai-expect-description-text-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      font-size: {{ block.settings.description_size_desktop }}px;
    }
  }
{% endstyle %}

<what-you-can-expect-{{ ai_gen_id }} class="ai-expect-section-{{ ai_gen_id }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
  <div class="ai-expect-container-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
    <div class="ai-expect-header-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
      <h2 class="ai-expect-heading-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
        <span class="ai-expect-heading-normal-{{ ai_gen_id }}">{{ block.settings.heading_part_1 }}</span> <span class="ai-expect-heading-accent-{{ ai_gen_id }}">{{ block.settings.heading_part_2 }}</span>
      </h2>
      {% if block.settings.subtext != blank %}
        <p class="ai-expect-subtext-{{ ai_gen_id }}">{{ block.settings.subtext }}</p>
      {% endif %}
    </div>

    <div class="ai-expect-phases-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
      <div class="ai-expect-phase-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
        <div class="ai-expect-image-column-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
          <div class="ai-expect-image-wrapper-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
            {% if block.settings.phase_1_image %}
              <img
                src="{{ block.settings.phase_1_image | image_url: width: 600 }}"
                alt="{{ block.settings.phase_1_image.alt | escape }}"
                class="ai-expect-image-{{ ai_gen_id }}"
                loading="lazy"
                width="{{ block.settings.phase_1_image.width }}"
                height="{{ block.settings.phase_1_image.height }}"
              >
            {% else %}
              <div class="ai-expect-image-placeholder-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
                {{ 'image' | placeholder_svg_tag }}
              </div>
            {% endif %}
          </div>
          <div class="ai-expect-label-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
            <div class="ai-expect-label-name-{{ ai_gen_id }}">{{ block.settings.phase_1_name }}</div>
            <div class="ai-expect-label-time-{{ ai_gen_id }}">{{ block.settings.phase_1_time }}</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="ai-expect-description-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
          <p class="ai-expect-description-text-{{ ai_gen_id }}">{{ block.settings.phase_1_description }}</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="ai-expect-phase-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
        <div class="ai-expect-image-column-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
          <div class="ai-expect-image-wrapper-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
            {% if block.settings.phase_2_image %}
              <img
                src="{{ block.settings.phase_2_image | image_url: width: 600 }}"
                alt="{{ block.settings.phase_2_image.alt | escape }}"
                class="ai-expect-image-{{ ai_gen_id }}"
                loading="lazy"
                width="{{ block.settings.phase_2_image.width }}"
                height="{{ block.settings.phase_2_image.height }}"
              >
            {% else %}
              <div class="ai-expect-image-placeholder-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
                {{ 'image' | placeholder_svg_tag }}
              </div>
            {% endif %}
          </div>
          <div class="ai-expect-label-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
            <div class="ai-expect-label-name-{{ ai_gen_id }}">{{ block.settings.phase_2_name }}</div>
            <div class="ai-expect-label-time-{{ ai_gen_id }}">{{ block.settings.phase_2_time }}</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="ai-expect-description-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
          <p class="ai-expect-description-text-{{ ai_gen_id }}">{{ block.settings.phase_2_description }}</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="ai-expect-phase-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
        <div class="ai-expect-image-column-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
          <div class="ai-expect-image-wrapper-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
            {% if block.settings.phase_3_image %}
              <img
                src="{{ block.settings.phase_3_image | image_url: width: 600 }}"
                alt="{{ block.settings.phase_3_image.alt | escape }}"
                class="ai-expect-image-{{ ai_gen_id }}"
                loading="lazy"
                width="{{ block.settings.phase_3_image.width }}"
                height="{{ block.settings.phase_3_image.height }}"
              >
            {% else %}
              <div class="ai-expect-image-placeholder-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
                {{ 'image' | placeholder_svg_tag }}
              </div>
            {% endif %}
          </div>
          <div class="ai-expect-label-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
            <div class="ai-expect-label-name-{{ ai_gen_id }}">{{ block.settings.phase_3_name }}</div>
            <div class="ai-expect-label-time-{{ ai_gen_id }}">{{ block.settings.phase_3_time }}</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="ai-expect-description-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
          <p class="ai-expect-description-text-{{ ai_gen_id }}">{{ block.settings.phase_3_description }}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</what-you-can-expect-{{ ai_gen_id }}>

<script>
  (function() {
    class WhatYouCanExpect{{ ai_gen_id }} extends HTMLElement {
      constructor() {
        super();
      }

      connectedCallback() {
      }
    }

    customElements.define('what-you-can-expect-{{ ai_gen_id }}', WhatYouCanExpect{{ ai_gen_id }});
  })();
</script>

